WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.110
2006.

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.510
Greenpeace publishes a report
called Eating up the Amazon.

3
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:11.550
It linked fast-food and supermarket chains
to soy grown on destroyed Amazon rainforest.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.850
Ten years later, researchers set
out to measure what had changed.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.450
Can civil society change
how global companies behave?

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.310
Or do companies simply ignore campaigners?

7
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.190
In this mission, you'll follow the
campaign through global supply chains,

8
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.470
and judge whose evidence of its
effects is most independent.

9
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.130
Then you'll study a second
campaign, on garment factory safety,

10
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.850
and see why experts and the
public rank risks so differently.

11
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.430
Your mission: evaluate whether civil society
can change how global companies behave.
